\par
Decision support tool
\par
The aim of this study is to describe the development and application of a web-based decision support
\par
tool (ViRTUE) for performing climate risk evaluations of water supply systems. The tool is designed for
\par
small-scale water utilities in the northeastern United States that may lack the resources for detailed
\par
climate change risk investigations. Development of this tool demonstrates a relatively new approach to
\par
web application development using the Shiny framework for the R programming language to create an
\par
interactive environment for stakeholders and water managers to explore climate vulnerabilities. Using a
\par
decision-scaling framework, the tool allows the user to perform a climate stress test to evaluate the
\par
performance and vulnerability to water supply shortfalls of local reservoir systems over a wide range of
\par
potential climate change scenarios using a generic systems model. Probabilities of future climate con-
\par
ditions derived from climate projections then help inform utility operators of impending risk.
