4. Case study: Spring eld water and sewer commission
\par
To demonstrate an application of ViRTUE, we present a case
\par
study using the Spring eld Water and Sewer Commission's
\par
(SWSC) water supply system. The reservoir system, located in the
\par
West eld River Basin in Central Massachusetts, consists of three
\par
major reservoirs: Cobble Mountain Reservoir (total storage at
\par
max elevation is 22,829 MG), Borden Brook Reservoir (2500 MG),
\par
and Littleville Reservoir (10,560 MG). The SWSC serves a popu-
\par
lation of approximately 250,000 people in Massachusetts,
\par
including the municipalities of Agawam, East Longmeadow,
\par
Ludlow, West eld, and Spring eld. For the purposes of this
\par
analysis, Cobble Mountain Reservoir was treated as the system's
\par
major storage reservoir, with in ows from surface runoff, direct
\par
precipitation, and the Borden Brook Reservoir located upstream.
\par
The Borden Brook Reservoir was excluded from the analysis
\par
because it has minimal active operation and primarily functions
\par
as a run-of-river facility.
\par
