\par
With respect to SCM performance, items relate to observable outcomes or improvements either in the form of increased profit
\par
or customer satisfaction, or decreased overall costs or breakdowns in SCM processes (i.e., Wamba et al., 2015; Brinch, 2018;
\par
Manyika et al., 2011; Waller and Fawcett, 2013). Finally, we measure items (see Table 2) relating to a firm's business strategy
\par
and culture using a slider, with the constructs positioned on a continuum, so that responses align towards one extremity or
\par
the other, but not both at the same time.
