Proposition 5. For both attack types, security information sharing
\par
is an effective economic incentive that not only can improve an
\par
interconnected firm's security level but also can reduce its total
\par
expected cost. An interconnected firm's optimal investment
\par
increases with the network vulnerability only when the portion
\par
of security information sharing is greater than an ``effective value''.
\par
This proposition provides an interconnected firm with
\par
inspiration to adopt the mechanism of security information
\par
sharing. First, sharing security information is always beneficial
\par
and can improve the level of information security as well as
\par
reduce the total expected cost. Second, sharing information
\par
internalises the negative externality of interconnection and
\par
encourages firms to invest more in security only when the por-
\par
tion of security information sharing is greater than the ``effec-
\par
tive value''. Thus, in order to overcome the negative
\par
externality of interconnection, some associations like CERT
\par
Coordination Centre can play a coordinating role by stipulating
\par
that any member has to follow the rule that each member's
\par
portion of security information sharing should be greater than
\par
the ``effective value''.
