\textbf{4.1. Research Questions}
\par
\textbf{Main Question of Study}
\par
Can a senior manager be a deviation factor in management forecasting?
\par
\textbf{Sub-Questions of study}
\par
Are optimistic biases the main cause of deviation in management forecasting?
\par
Are pessimistic biases the main causes of deviation in management forecasting?
\par
Can voluntary disclosure of forecasting be an accuracy factor in forecasting?
\par
\textbf{5. The Meta-Analysis Results of the Research Questions}
\par
\textbf{5.1. Main question: Can a Senior Manager be a Deviation Factor in Management Forecasting?}
\par
A meta-analysis of reviewed studies has identified that 19 cases of factors that caused the deviation of management
\par
forecasts are issues related to the Executive Director, so the answer is yes, and the senior manager of organization can be
\par
one of the main reasons for deviation from the forecasts of the management (Table 3).
