\textbf{Second Round: Evaluation of the Typology}
\par
The process of validation depends to a large extent on the
\par
nature of the research (Emory \& Cooper, 1991). In the present
\par
research, the proposed framework is based on literature review
\par
and conceptual theorizing. As such, theory is a profound ele-
\par
ment in designing and conceptualizing the model (Walshan,
\par
1995). For the process of validation, we then decided to use
\par
empirical evidence to ensure reliability and confidence in using
\par
the model in practice. We assessed the adequacy and strength
\par
of the proposed typology against the criteria proposed by Hunt
\par
(1991). According to Hunt (1991), five criteria should be used
\par
to justify whether or not a typology is adequate: (1) Is the
\par
phenomenon to be classified adequately specified? (2) Is the
\par
classification characteristic adequately specified? (3) Are the
\par
categories mutually exclusive? (4) Is the typology collectively
\par
exhaustive? (5) Is the typology useful?
\par
Almost all of the interviewees could understand and explain
\par
