IT investments on firm productivity and innovation out-
\par
put, IT business value, organizational complementarities,
\par
determinants of R\&D collaboration, innovative behavior
\par
of firms, external knowledge spillovers, government policy
\par
failures, and sustainable energy innovations. His work has
\par
appeared in journals such as \emph{Research Policy, Industrial and}
\par
\emph{Corporate Change, Small Business Economics, Ecological}
\par
\emph{Economics, Ambio, Review of World Economics}, and \emph{Kyklos}.
\par
\textbf{AUTHOR BIOS}
\par
Fardad Zand is an assistant professor at the Technology,
\par
Strategy and Entrepreneurship Department of Delft
\par
University of Technology. He is affiliated with the MIT
\par
Center for Digital Business in Cambridge, USA. He holds
\par
two BCs (with honors) in Chemical Engineering and
\par
Computer Science, a MSc (with honors) in Management
\par
of Technology, and a PhD (with honors) in Information
\par
Economics. His work has been published in journals such as
\par
the \emph{Journal of Production Innovation Management (JPIM)}.
\par
His research has also earned him two best paper awards
