4.1. Summary of the geology and hydrogeology
\par
Principally, the main rock types found on the island of
\par
\"Asp\"o are the \"Asp\"o diorites consisting of granodiorite,
\par
quartzmonzodiorite and quartzrich diorite, and the \"Avr\"o-
\par
granites consisting of granite to granodiorite. In addition,
\par
there are minor inclusions of mafic rock types, such as
\par
gabbro, in the area, as well as veins of fine-grained
\par
granite, more often in the \"Asp\"odiorites than in the
\par
\"Avr\"ogranites (Rh\'en et al. 1997). Most fractures are
\par
oriented northwest--southeast, although the majority of
\par
the shear zones are oriented southwest--northeast (Ber-
\par
glund et al. 2003). Most of the zones have a higher
\par
hydraulic conductivity than the surrounding rock
\par
mass (Morosini and Hultgren 2012). Hydraulic tests
\par
conducted during drilling of the investigation bore-
\par
holes KA2051A01 and KA3007A01 showed that the
