4.2. Decision alternatives and objective of investigation
\par
There are two possible positions for the TAS04 niche,
\par
and the most suitable position must be found in order to
\par
meet the groundwater requirement and the demand for
\par
no pre-grouting. Even though the plan is to construct the
\par
tunnel without grouting, there is a risk that grouting will
\par
be needed anyway in order to maintain the groundwater
\par
level in the area. Taking this risk into account, the
\par
decision-maker has two options: either to prepare for
\par
grouting and order equipment and material in case of a
\par
groundwater depression, or to construct the tunnel
\par
without any grouting preparations and solve the pro-
\par
blems on site if they arise. This produces four specific
\par
decision alternatives:
\par
(1) Position 1, prepare for grouting.
\par
(2) Position 1, do not prepare for grouting.
\par
(3) Position 2, prepare for grouting.
\par
(4) Position 2, do not prepare for grouting.
\par
Hence, there are two null alternatives (Ni), when
\par
grouting is not prepared, and two action alternatives
\par
(Ai), when grouting is prepared in each alternative
\par
position of the niche, i = 1,2. Failure, Fi, means that
\par
the tunnelling activities in any of the two positions, i,
\par
would cause more than 5 m depression in the observa-
\par
tion borehole, KA2050A.
\par
The purpose of the VOIA is to find out if it is
\par
economically justifiable to drill an additional investiga-
\par
tion borehole (KA3065A01 in Figure 3) as part of
\par
deciding on the location of the TAS04 niche, and the
\par
decision regarding grouting preparations. The investiga-
\par
tion boreholes at \"Asp\"o HRL have several purposes in
\par
the sense that the results from the investigations will
\par
be used for different subject areas. For hydrogeological
\par
issues, the purpose of the investigations in borehole
\par
KA3065A01 is to determine the hydraulic conditions
\par
